Held 2026-08-31, before it ran.

Queuing this was the wrong order and would have wasted about $13.86.

The publish is blocked by FIVE things, and the page gate is one:

    STOP  page gate            3 unjudged sentences        ~$13.86
    STOP  email gate           4 unjudged sentences        ~$3.10
    STOP  outside review       4 changes with no decision  free
    STOP  every quotation is recorded   1 unrecorded       free
    STOP  quotation sources were opened 15 unattested      free

Running the gates first clears two of five and leaves three. Worse, the free
work CHANGES THE PAGE -- filling quotation records is fine, but any correction
that follows from the outside-review decisions adds sentences the gate has not
read, which invalidates the run that was just paid for.

Free work first, then one gate run at the end, on final text. That is the same
batching argument made three hours ago about not paying $20 for four re-gates
of the same page -- and I queued this one anyway.
